Original commit body from de2812496ed8259aeb8a6b589d7844bed5fe443e:

scala.yaml had no stdio rows, so a bare println(secret) -- the commonest
stdout write in scala -- matched nothing and a never-logs-a-secret claim
read `confirmed` with no caveat.

- scala.yaml: logging rows for scala.Predef println/print/printf and
  scala.Console println/print/printf + attributes out/err; ipc_recv for
  Console.in.
- scala.py: _scala_static_owner adds the objects scala._ imports
  implicitly (Console, Predef) after the import and java.lang's list; a
  project type or an import of the name keeps its own answer.
  Console.out/err receivers are typed java.io.PrintStream with
  io_target_kind std_stream, as System.out/err are (WI-rabum), and read
  as values they are module_attr_refs on scala.Console.
- tests/test_citation_gate_tests.py: the citation-family size bound now
  applies to the hop-2 surface (source/script citers, 15) instead of all
  citers (47, over the 40 bound on dev already): a test citer -- e.g. a
  `# covers:` declaration -- selects only itself.

Measured against dev (classified findings): sbt +179 logging, gatling
+20, lila +10; 0 lost, every addition logging.

